' bug-466 Reproduction 4: `IMPORT udp` is never referenced, yet it used to make
' this otherwise-identical program BUILD — `udp` declares a record whose field is
' a `net::Address`, which dragged `Address`'s definition into the project-wide
' type table. Whether a program compiled depended on which unrelated packages it
' imported. The verdict must now be the same with or without this import.
IMPORT tcp
IMPORT udp

FUNC main AS Integer
  RES s = tcp::listen("127.0.0.1", 0)
  LET b = tcp::localAddress(s)
  RES c = tcp::connect("127.0.0.1", b.port)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
